This is the same operational model as Claude Code.<p><pre><code>  ls ~&#x2F;.local&#x2F;share&#x2F;claude&#x2F;versions&#x2F;
  ps auxww | grep &quot;claude bg&quot;
</code></pre>
I see a few prior versions of the Claude Code binary and several running background tasks, without any copy of Claude Code in the foreground. I regularly get a &quot;Update available&quot; message in my Claude Code UI too.

while this points it out, i&#x27;ll show you what I had in place:<p>~&#x2F;.codex&#x2F;config.toml<p><pre><code>    [features]
    daemon_auto_start = false
</code></pre>
hell, I also have this redundancy configured in bash:<p><pre><code>    codex() {
      command codex --no-daemon &quot;${@:-.}&quot;
    }</code></pre>
